{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude","id":474764,"title":"How big can you grow with Vicissitude?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T13:02:20-07:00","id":474764,"title":"How big can you grow with Vicissitude?","content":"How much mass can you grow with Vicissitude? There have been examples of characters who have used it for this purpose, but no rules for it I can think of, other then adding the Huge Size Merit.<br /> <br /> Are there other powers/effects that can also increase a target's mass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:16:23-07:00","id":474798,"title":"","content":"I've always ruled that Vicissitude cannot alter mass, just move things around and stretch size. At least without the elder power Graft Life to Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:39:26-07:00","id":474878,"title":"","content":"Aside from the mass gained from Horrid Form and Chitoprean Marauder I have also ruled it like the squirrel:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I've always ruled that Vicissitude cannot alter mass, just move things around and stretch size. At least without the elder power Graft Life to Life.</span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:51:49-07:00","id":474999,"title":"","content":"What level of Vicissitude is needed to fuse to bodies into one? The example I'm thinking of is a Toreador who wanted to fuse a human and a horse to make a centaur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:03:35-07:00","id":475010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=474999#post474999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of Vicissitude is needed to fuse to bodies into one? The example I'm thinking of is a Toreador who wanted to fuse a human and a horse to make a centaur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 6, Graft Life to Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1916-vertical8","name":"Vertical8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:46:59-07:00","id":475108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vertical8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=475010#post475010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Level 6, Graft Life to Life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's such a useful power. Most useful vicissitude power, honestly.<br /> <br /> But you'll absolutely see some sketchy descriptions in char sheets, tzimisce with only the first three levels of vicissitude fusing together their enemies, making massive monster-wolves when they're basically incapable of making the wolves stronger without taking away other stats or health, bone plating without considering where, exactly, that bone comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:21:45-07:00","id":475173,"title":"","content":"While I agree with everything stated above about vicissitude not being able to alter mass, if you only want to get bigger/bulkier, I don't really see why vicissitude wouldn't be able to alter the density of flesh, especially muscle, since such tissues vary in density in a normal human body as well. Granted, such changes in density are marginal at best, but maybe vicissitude would be able to have a more profound effect. Of course, this would require making some judgement calls in biomechanics and such. For example, elongating a bone by making it less dense would greatly reduce its structural strength (not to mention that being longer, the torque generated by forces applied at the ends would be bigger as well), which would result in it breaking much more easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5246-warlock","name":"Warlock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:09:45-07:00","id":475368,"title":"","content":"Yeah, without the ability to add more body parts to yourself, you <i>can't</i> use Vicissitude to gain mass. It's just not possible. It's a sculpting Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T01:26:15-07:00","id":475542,"title":"","content":"I figure you should be able to add the equivalent weight of the blood you expend on flesh/bonecraft in body mass.<br /> Canonically, there are a number of 'unenlightened', more martial Tzimisce who just kept adding on bone plating and muscle mass far beyond mortal size constraints.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5520-hideamuro","name":"Hideamuro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T03:11:33-07:00","id":475578,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's White Wolf. Their authors never paid <i>too</i> much attention to things like &quot;rules&quot; when it came to writing up NPCs and metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T04:12:14-07:00","id":475602,"title":"","content":"I've ruled it the same as everyone else. My feeling is that to increase mass (you can certainly stretch out what's already there, but this would only spread out existing mass), you'd need to physically graft new flesh to the body a la vozhd and other creatures. This can be done, but is an application of Graft Life to Life.<br /> <br /> I've always assumed those less skilled Tzimisce who've been radically altered beyond their own powers, and/or who possess war ghouls, have been helped along/mutilated/tortured by their sires/mentors/angry superiors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:46:50-07:00","id":475662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude#post474764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much mass can you grow with Vicissitude? There have been examples of characters who have used it for this purpose, but no rules for it I can think of, other then adding the Huge Size Merit.<br /> <br /> Are there other powers/effects that can also increase a target's mass?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You've got a guy living in the sewers who's the size of a city...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:57:43-07:00","id":475672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=475368#post475368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, without the ability to add more body parts to yourself, you <i>can't</i> use Vicissitude to gain mass. It's just not possible. It's a sculpting Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as others noted, Horrid Form can add mass temporarily.<br /> <br /> Could it be assumed that at level 4 you can add/alter mass?<br /> <br /> Also, are there other Disciplines/Rituals/powers/effects that can add mass to targets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:40:21-07:00","id":475858,"title":"","content":"Sanguinus can trade it around between Blood Brothers or merge them into one big blob. Protean can make you bigger at higher levels, and I suppose Gangrel can choose a larger-than-human combat form with 4 dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=475662#post475662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got a guy living in the sewers who's the size of a city...</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Eldest Fiend didn't just snap its fingers and POOF! grow to gigantic size. The implication is it's been absorbing everything it can get its tentacles on in the New York underground for years\u2014maybe since the mid 70s?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:06:45-07:00","id":475913,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely convinced even Horrid Form actually adds mass. It twists the body, maximising its efficiency by taking all the unused bulk (in the case of vampires this includes most of the internal organs) and applying it directly to muscle mass while at the same time stretching the frame to appear to increase in size. At least that's how I've always seen it. Adding mass just seems very out of flavour for Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of increasing density though. I can absolutely buy that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:40:34-07:00","id":475940,"title":"","content":"Actually, Malleable Viasage allows for a small height alteration: a foot, or 30cm. That's quite enough to make someone significantly taller or smaller. Fleshcraft can be used to do the same to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:31:19-07:00","id":476201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=475940#post475940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Malleable Viasage allows for a small height alteration: a foot, or 30cm. That's quite enough to make someone significantly taller or smaller. Fleshcraft can be used to do the same to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And as far as I know, the rules <i>never</i> stated Vicissitude is limited by the law about conservation of mass (such law might make sense in Masquerade, but did not in Dark Ages).<br /> <br /> Yes it's a common hack/house rule, but I think the question was about the rules (which in Vampire include non rule canon material, given that the rules aren't that precise).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing on <a href=\"https://tousrolistes.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">French Online virtual tabletop rpg community</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3723-blacky","name":"Blacky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3723_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:18:46-07:00","id":476233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/474764-how-big-can-you-grow-with-vicissitude?p=475602#post475602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed those less skilled Tzimisce who've been radically altered beyond their own powers, and/or who possess war ghouls, have been helped along/mutilated/tortured by their sires/mentors/angry superiors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except a lot of character backgrounds specifically state otherwise - like Marelle, here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Marelle\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Marelle</a><br /> <br /> A tzimisce with only 3 in Vicissitude who goes around with her wolf ghouls &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">of</span></span></span>ten combining the skeletons <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">and organs of several at once&quot; </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:37:16-07:00","id":476250,"title":"","content":"I suppose it would be physically possible for someone to graft a few animals together with Vicissitude 3, but they'd still be individual animals, like rat kings or two-headed snakes, that would have to learn to work together in guiding their fused bodies rather than being truly merged into a single being as is the case with vozhd. I bet they wouldn't tend to be very long-lived either, organ rejection would probably set in quickly and kill most such fusions.<br /> <br /> Someone who knows that ritual Virstania developed as a prelude to creating Gargoyles would be able to make viable animal fusions, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T16:25:09-07:00","id":476382,"title":"","content":"That's really the key Matt. Lower Vicissitude can slap two creatures together and meld the flesh, but it doesn't grant one control over the other. Furthermore, with Vicissitude 3, I can rip off one guy's arm and graft it onto another guy, but that doesn't make it his arm or let him control it. Graft Life to Life lets the addition actually function for the recipient. That's the difference.<br /> <br /> As to height alterations, you are absolutely right. However, 6&quot; is not that much and certainly does not require the addition of mass to achieve. It would be quite easy to add or remove 6&quot; just by juggling about excess tissue and increasing or decreasing density.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T14:26:00-07:00","id":477322,"title":"","content":"I think killersquirrel59 put it most succinctly, but to pull some examples from the text itself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Malleable Visage<br /> A vampire with this power may alter her own bodily parameters ... Such changes are <b>cosmetic*</b> and minor in scope ... She must physically mold the alteration, <b>literally shaping her flesh**</b> into the desired result. </div> </div> </div>*i.e., non-functional<br /> **shaping =/= creation/generation/addition<br /> <br /> And again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Fleshcraft<br /> This power is similar to Malleable Visage ... A vampire may use this power to <b>move clumps of skin, fat, and muscle tissue***</b>, thus providing additional padding where needed. </div> </div> </div>***again, moving =/= creation/generation/addition<br /> <br /> Ergo, the rules don't seem to support the creation of new tissue. The mass seems to remain constant, and merely be reworked/shifted around, until the higher powers.<br /> <br /> And while Vicissitude 2 and 3 do allow the fusion of bodies together, they wouldn't share any kind of consciousness, and would be separate beings joined together (with potential issues around organ failure and rejection, although you may rule that doesn't happen because magic). You can't move <b>working</b> limbs and new, <b>functional</b> tissue from one being onto another until Vicissitude 6. You can only change their appearance or move things around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T06:50:35-07:00","id":479019,"title":"","content":"Well there's the matter of what type of flesh they can manipulate. If they can do everything that a doctor can do but with their hands and mystical connections bypassing the need for healing times, they can connect nerve tissue and allow for control of a newly grafted limb (though they might get issues if incompatibility or maybe not because of mysticalness). I'd probably house rule it to spending blood to add mass, in a sort of mystical transformation.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's all really up to ST and is much more open ended in ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:20:35-07:00","id":479623,"title":"","content":"The existence of a level 6 power specifically to perform the function of mixing two living beings together suggests that level 3 cannot do that. Otherwise the level 6 could not exist. One would also think that if level 2+3 could do so, it would say so.<br /> <br /> However, since Vicissitude has essentially no rules and no well defined limits, one could also argue that level 2+3 does not say it <i>can't</i> do that, and be on just as solid ground. Hurray!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T06:30:41-07:00","id":1510878,"title":"","content":"Ghouls can regrow lost limbs, organs and body parts. It requires a lot of Vitae and a Stamina roll, but if the ghoul is really determined ( spends Willpower ) he should make it.<br /> A reasonably skilled surgeon can remove muscles and bones <i><b>surgically, without Vicissitude</b></i> so the ghoul can regrow them, and use the removed tissues - with Vicissitude - to enhace the overall mass moving them to other parts of the body. It takes time, skill and effort, but it can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T13:09:41-07:00","id":1511013,"title":"","content":"Let's go against the grain. <br /> <br /> Not directly, but yes, you should be able make someone more massive with Vicissitude. Shapers practice forms of medicine that ordinary practitioners wouldn't dare to, because &quot;do no harm&quot; doesn't apply to Tzmisce, and &quot;should I do it&quot; is seen as a petty weakness when the only question you should be asking is &quot;can I do it&quot;. A thousand missing pets later, the answer should be yes. <br /> <br /> -Deliberately causing Gigantism or Acromegaly by messing with the pituitary gland, causing human growth hormone to go wild. Possibly, a masterful tzmisce could reopen growth plates, allowing for the former post puterty <br /> - adding mass the natural way (lots of food, or blood transfusions) then transforming mass to parts of the body it shouldn't be in, perhaps changing it's form, while the missing piece gets replaced by the added mass. <br /> As Condradine suggests, removing, ghoul or other magical method for healing, and then reattaching.. <br /> <br /> You can also just whack foreign substances in. I'm not talking about life-to-life but like, new custom built bones, natural or metal, devices... and while you can't directly shape an organ transplant into the body you can use vicissitude to make opening the person up easier: presumably once the organ has been accepted by the body the shaper is free to modify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}